# Self-maintaining records

When an action introduces or changes a managed fact — a new asset, sub-processor/connector,
data flow, capability, or decision (or a material change to one) — stage the matching
register/document update in the SAME change, without waiting to be asked:

- assets → `governance/asset-inventory.yaml`; tools/services → `governance/suppliers.yaml`
- data flows → `governance/data-inventory.yaml` + `governance/ropa.yaml`
- decisions → an ADR in `docs/decisions/`

Route through normal PR/CI; never silently edit an approved document. If unsure which record
applies, flag it rather than skipping. Canonical norm: `records/SCHEMA.md` → "Maintenance norm".
Anything derivable from source is generated (`scripts/records/register.mjs`), not hand-maintained.
